     1	//! Function metadata — the 6.4-0 substrate shape (contract §10.2).
     2	//!
     3	//! **Status (2026-05-28): SUBSTRATE SHIPPED + 6.4-1 SUBSTRATE-COMPLETION
     4	//! LANDED.** `FunctionRegistry` carries `metadata: HashMap<String,
     5	//! FunctionMetadata>` (`ql-functions/src/registry.rs`), populated for every
     6	//! builtin via `register_builtin_metadata` at boot.
     7	//!
     8	//! **6.4-0 substrate (2026-05-28):** the two prior whitelists in
     9	//! `calcgraph_session.rs` (`is_volatile_function`,
    10	//! `is_address_only_reference_fn`) became thin migration shims that read
    11	//! `metadata.volatility ∈ {Volatile, Dynamic}` and `metadata.dep_shape ==
    12	//! AddressOnly` respectively — behavior preserved byte-for-byte against the
    13	//! prior hardcoded matchers. `FormulaDeps` gained `functions_used:
    14	//! Vec<Arc<str>>` and `CalcgraphSession` gained `functions_used:
    15	//! HashMap<Arc<str>, HashSet<NodeId>>` + two hooks (`on_function_registered`
    16	//! / `on_function_unregistered`) for contract §10.3 registration-
    17	//! invalidation.
    18	//!
    19	//! **6.4-1 substrate-completion (2026-05-28):** the two REMAINING
    20	//! whitelists in `ql-exec::plan` (`is_aggregate_function` `:406-505`,
    21	//! `is_reference_aware_function` `:566-571`) — which drove the binder's
    22	//! `arg_ctx` decision — now also derive from metadata. This required a new
    23	//! [`ArgContext`] axis (the binder-admission category), distinct from
    24	//! [`BatchShape`] (the eval-time call ABI — UDFs are `ArrayBatch`, builtin
    25	//! aggregates are still per-cell `Scalar` calls even though the binder
    26	//! admits range args). I1 added [`DepShape::LazyShape`] for ISREF so the
    27	//! walker's hardcoded `name == "ISREF"` short-circuit becomes metadata-
    28	//! derived. H3 added a PlanCache `fn_gen: u64` counter mirroring
    29	//! `name_gen`, so a `register_metadata` / `unregister_metadata` call
    30	//! invalidates the bind cache and the next eval re-extracts deps with the
    31	//! current metadata. The substrate hooks remain dirty-only at the
    32	//! `CalcgraphSession` layer — the H3 closure is the cache invalidation,
    33	//! not a per-dependent `reextract_deps` call.
    34	//!
    35	//! ## Metadata-update atomicity (I2)
    36	//!
    37	//! v1 policy is the **two-step contract**: clients MUST call
    38	//! `unregister_metadata(canonical_name)` then `register_metadata(new_meta)`
    39	//! to update an existing entry; there is NO atomic `update_metadata`
    40	//! today. The transient window between the two calls leaves the function
    41	//! in the "unknown" state — formulas referencing it bind / re-bind with
    42	//! `Volatility::Dynamic` (the conservative default in contract §10.3), so
    43	//! the engine never serves a result computed against stale metadata. The
    44	//! binder's `arg_ctx` falls back to `Scalar` during the gap (a `=MYUDF(A1:
    45	//! A10)` call would surface `BindError::NamedRangeInScalarContext`); this
    46	//! is acceptable because (a) UDFs register at workspace-trust elevation,
    47	//! a transient window during a known reload event; (b) atomic in-place
    48	//! swap on a HashMap is straightforward to add when a real UDF live-edit
    49	//! flow needs it, and the two-step path keeps the substrate small. 6.4
    50	//! may add `update_metadata` as a non-breaking superset; the two-step
    51	//! path remains supported.
    52	//!
    53	//! Cross-refs: `docs/api/session-api.md` §10 (function metadata contract),
    54	//! `docs/phase6/6-4-entry-plan.md` §2 (the H1+H3+M+I scope of 6.4-1),
    55	//! `docs/audits/2026-05-28-6-4-0-substrate-audit/SYNTHESIS.md` (substrate
    56	//! audit + the 6.4-1 dispositions).
