  1004	        //     ought to be idempotent (rule 5), but unconditional
  1005	        //     `is_this_row` would narrow it to formula row →
  1006	        //     `#VALUE!` for any formula not in the header row.
  1007	        //   - `@Sales[#All]` / multi-column refs — semantics differ;
  1008	        //     resolve_structured_ref already returns `is_this_row:
  1009	        //     true` for `ThisRowColumn`/`ThisRowColumnRange` and
  1010	        //     `false` for the special-form combinations that
  1011	        //     resolve to single cells / multi-axis ranges. The
  1012	        //     `@` operator should respect that classification, not
  1013	        //     force-override.
  1014	        //
  1015	        // Discrimination is by spec shape:
  1016	        //   - `BareColumn(_)` → @ overrides to true (the load-bearing
