  1489	    // `debug_assert!` to `assert!` — a release build that hits this
  1490	    // failure now panics at registry construction (boot time) rather
  1491	    // than silently shipping with broken walker invariants. Cost is
  1492	    // one O(n) walk at boot (n=260; ~µs); the alternative is that a
  1493	    // future contributor adding a `r.register*` call without a
  1494	    // matching metadata entry ships a release binary with silent
  1495	    // unknown-fn fallback for that built-in. The boot-time fail-loud
  1496	    // matches the No-Fallbacks rule.
  1497	    assert!(
  1498	        r.fns.keys().all(|name| r.metadata.contains_key(*name)),
