   500	  the cursor — so pull pollers and push subscribers never starve each other. Retention is a bounded
   501	  window; if a consumer falls behind the horizon, the page carries `dropped:true` + a
   502	  `FullResyncRequired` event (the consumer reseeds via `snapshot()`), rather than silently losing
   503	  events. Ordering: an `OperationCompleted{op_id}` event never precedes the events produced by that op.
   504	- `Diagnostic` is the same DTO whether returned synchronously (`validate_formula`) or via the stream.
   505	
   506	---
   507	
   508	## 10. Function metadata & graph-invalidation contract (R-P6-4 / 6.4-0)
   509	
   510	### 10.1 The gap (CLOSED by 6.4-0 substrate, 2026-05-28; commits `ac20a432c63` + audit-fix `63592126afe`)
   511	**Pre-substrate (historical):** `FunctionRegistry` (`ql-functions/src/registry.rs`) stored **dispatch only**.
   512	Volatility + reference-shape lived in **two hardcoded whitelists** in `calcgraph_session.rs`
   513	(`is_volatile_function` `:149-164`; `is_address_only_reference_fn` `:201-203`); `FormulaDeps`
   514	had no `functions_used` reverse index. A Python UDF couldn't be added to a hardcoded match,
   515	and a registration/metadata change couldn't dirty its callers → silent graph bypass.
   516	
   517	**Post-substrate (6.4-0 SHIPPED 2026-05-28):**
   518	- `FunctionRegistry` carries a first-class `metadata: HashMap<String, FunctionMetadata>` keyed by
   519	  canonical (ASCII-uppercase) name; populated for every builtin via `register_builtin_metadata`
   520	  at `default_registry()` tail. Public API: `metadata(name)` / `register_metadata(meta)` /
   521	  `unregister_metadata(name)` / `iter_metadata()` / `metadata_count()`. Dispatched-builtin
   522	  unregister is REFUSED (`FunctionRegistryError::Conflict`) — preserves the migration-shim
   523	  invariant. Boot-time `assert!` enforces "every dispatched fn has metadata."
   524	- `FormulaDeps` gained `functions_used: Vec<Arc<str>>`; walker pushes at the TOP of the
   525	  `ExprPlan::Function` arm so address-only / ISREF / nested-function paths all record uniformly.
   526	- `CalcgraphSession` gained `functions_used: HashMap<Arc<str>, HashSet<NodeId>>` (mirror of
   527	  `name_to_formulas`) + two hooks `on_function_registered(name)` / `on_function_unregistered(name)`
   528	  with transitive BFS-fanout (same Phase 3.10 H2 pattern as `on_set_name`). Storage gate was
   529	  widened to also store `formula_deps` when only `names`/`tables`/`functions_used` are populated
   530	  (closes the latent `ROW(MyName)` cleanup bug).
   531	- The two prior whitelists are now thin migration shims (`is_volatile_function(registry, name)` →
   532	  `metadata.volatility ∈ {Volatile, Dynamic}`; `is_address_only_reference_fn(registry, name)` →
   533	  `metadata.dep_shape == AddressOnly`). Behavior is preserved byte-for-byte against the prior
   534	  matchers.
   535	
   536	**STILL OPEN at 6.4 entry (block-on-entry must-fix; see audit-fix `63592126afe` + synthesis at `docs/audits/2026-05-28-6-4-0-substrate-audit/SYNTHESIS.md` + entry plan at `docs/phase6/6-4-entry-plan.md`):**
   537	- **H1** — `ql-exec::plan` carries two more hardcoded `matches!` whitelists
   538	  (`is_aggregate_function` `plan.rs:406-505`, `is_reference_aware_function` `plan.rs:566-571`)
   539	  that drive the binder's `arg_ctx` decision. UDFs with range args (every
   540	  `BatchShape::ArrayBatch` UDF) won't bind until these also derive from registry metadata. The
   541	  6.4-0 substrate is "two-thirds of the UDF prerequisite"; H1 is the missing third.
   542	- **H3** — register/unregister hooks dirty + transitive-fan but DO NOT re-extract deps. Contract
   543	  §10.3 ("re-extract deps + reschedule") requires both halves. The substrate hook is the
   544	  building block; 6.4 carries the orchestration via either (a) `fn_gen: u64` counter on
   545	  `crates/ql-exec/src/plan_cache.rs` (mirror `name_gen` at `:69-74`; bump per register/unregister;
   546	  cache miss triggers re-bind + fresh `FormulaDeps`), or (b) per-dependent `reextract_deps(node,
   547	  cached_plan, workbook, registry)` in the `WorkbookSession::register_function` orchestrator.
   548	
   549	### 10.2 `FunctionMetadata` (built in 6.4-0; v1 DTO now)
   550	```
   551	FunctionMetadata {
   552	  canonical_name: String,        // ASCII-UPPERCASE, matches parser canonicalization (ast.rs:54)
   553	  display_name: String?, aliases: [String]?,   // documented Unicode/alias policy
   554	  arity: Arity, volatility: Volatility,         // Pure | Volatile | Dynamic
   555	  determinism: bool, dep_shape: DepShape,       // Value-deps | AddressOnly | Custom(explicit deps)
   556	  batch_shape: BatchShape,                       // Scalar | Arrow/array batch (UDFs: batch from day one)
   557	  arg_policy: ArgPolicy, cancellation: CancelPolicy,  // cooperative | worker-kill
   558	  provenance_tags: [String],
   559	}
   560	```
   561	The two hardcoded whitelists become **derived** from registered metadata (built-ins register their
   562	true metadata; the whitelists remain only as a migration shim).
   563	
   564	### 10.3 Registration + invalidation rules (HIGH-5)
   565	- **Canonical name:** ASCII-uppercase; `register_function` normalizes + validates against the parser's
   566	  canonicalization. Unicode/alias policy documented.
   567	- **Collision rules:** `register_function` **returns an error** (not a panic) on collision with a
   568	  built-in, an existing UDF, or (if applicable) a name/table — `EngineError{class:Conflict,
   569	  code:"function_exists"}`.
   570	- **`functions_used` reverse index** *(new `FormulaDeps` field + graph map)*: the dep walker records
   571	  each function a formula calls; the graph keeps `function -> [formula nodes]`.
   572	- **Invalidation:** `register_function` / `unregister_function` / metadata-update **dirties every
   573	  formula referencing that canonical name** (re-extract deps + reschedule). This also covers formulas
   574	  that bound while the name was **unknown** and become valid on registration.
   575	- **Unknown-function policy:** a formula referencing an unregistered name is **graph-visible and
   576	  treated Volatile/Dynamic** (never silently Pure), so it recomputes once the UDF appears.
   577	
   578	### 10.4 Graph-invalidation model + exit tests (decision-lock §4)
   579	A UDF formula is a normal graph node; args walked + registered as deps via `mark_dirty_from_cell_write`
   580	(fanout `calcgraph_session.rs:~1396-1431`). Default Python UDFs are `Volatile`/`Dynamic` unless
   581	registered pure. `qb.publish()`/`qb.bind()` is the authoritative reactivity contract; `BoundFrame`
   582	edits dirty the **overlay** nodes; connector/file refresh dirties by **source revision**. **Exit tests
   583	(before 6.4 closes):** (1) pure UDF recomputes on referenced-input change; (2) pure UDF does NOT
   584	recompute on unrelated edit; (3) volatile UDF recomputes on recalc/volatile pass; (4) `publish` dirties
   585	dependents; (5) `BoundFrame` overlay edit dirties bound-range formulas; (6) canceled/timed-out UDF
   586	does not commit a late result; (7) failed UDF → deterministic `CellDiagnostic`; **(8, new)** registering
   587	a UDF dirties formulas that referenced its (previously-unknown) name.
   588	
   589	---
