1a7dfee12b03d03ea73678e00027638df969220f
feat(quantbook): Phase 6.4-1 substrate-completion -- H1 binder migration + H3 PlanCache fn_gen + M1/M3/M5/I1/I2

Block-on-6.4-entry HIGHs + filed substrate-completion items from the
6.4-0 audit (synthesis docs/audits/2026-05-28-6-4-0-substrate-audit/
SYNTHESIS.md) close in one cycle.

H1 (plan.rs binder whitelists -> metadata)
- New `ArgContext` axis on `FunctionMetadata` (`ql-session::function_meta`):
  Scalar / Aggregate / Reference. Mirrors the engine-internal
  `BindContext`; distinct from `BatchShape` (the eval-time call ABI —
  builtin aggregates stay Scalar-called per cell; UDFs declare ArrayBatch
  for Arrow IPC).
- `register_builtin_metadata` Phase 1 sets the 7 reference-aware names'
  arg_context to Reference. Phase 1.5 (new) sets the ~66 aggregate /
  range-aware / array-tier names' arg_context to Aggregate, mirroring
  the pre-6.4-1 `is_aggregate_function` matches! byte-for-byte.
- `ql-exec::plan::is_aggregate_function` and `is_reference_aware_function`
  drop their hardcoded matches! and read
  `registry.metadata(name).arg_context`. Signatures gain
  `&FunctionRegistry` — every binder entry point
  (`bind`, `bind_with_names`, `bind_with_names_and_sheets`,
  `bind_with_site`, `bind_with_site_no_tables`, `bind_with_context_v2`,
  `bind_implicit_intersection`) gains it too. Production callers
  (`WorkbookSession`, `WorkbookTransaction`, `WorkbookRuntime`,
  `CalcgraphSession::bind_text`) thread `self.registry`; tests pass
  `&default_registry()` (a shared `LazyLock<FunctionRegistry>` in
  `plan.rs::tests::TEST_REGISTRY` for the heavy users).

H3 (PlanCache fn_gen counter -- option A)
- `FunctionRegistry` gains `fn_gen: u64` + `fn_generation()` reader.
  Both `register_metadata` + `unregister_metadata` bump on success-only
  via `saturating_add(1)`; Conflict / NotFound failures leave the
  counter untouched (metadata table unchanged -> cache stays valid).
- `PlanCacheKey` gains `fn_gen: u64` between `name_gen` and
  `cell_anchor`. Five production call sites (`cells.rs:116, :521`,
  `recompute.rs:547, :753`, `tables.rs:825`) read
  `self.registry.fn_generation()` alongside
  `self.workbook.names().generation()`. Closes contract §10.3's
  "re-extract deps" half: 6.4-0 hooks dirty + reschedule; fn_gen
  invalidates the bind cache -> next eval re-binds with current metadata.

I1 (DepShape::LazyShape for ISREF)
- New `DepShape::LazyShape` variant in `function_meta.rs`. ISREF moves
  out of the AddressOnly batch (its Phase 1 override now sets
  `dep_shape: LazyShape`).
- New `is_lazy_shape_reference_fn(&registry, name)` migration shim in
  `calcgraph_session.rs`. Walker's hardcoded `name.as_ref() == "ISREF"`
  short-circuit becomes metadata-derived
  (`if is_lazy_shape_reference_fn(...) { /* skip arg walk */ }` before
  the address-only branch). Behavior preserved byte-for-byte.

I2 (metadata-update atomicity policy docs)
- `function_meta.rs` module header documents the two-step v1 policy
  (unregister + register, accepting the transient `#NAME?` window;
  6.4-0's conservative `Dynamic` default keeps formulas graph-visible
  during the gap; 6.4 may add `update_metadata` as a non-breaking
  superset).

M1 (FormulaDeps::is_empty/len API fix)
- `FormulaDeps::is_empty/len` now span all six tracked-dep fields
  (cells / named_ranges / names / tables / functions_used / is_volatile)
  instead of the 2-of-6 pre-6.4-1 lie. The substrate audit-fix's
  five-clause storage gate at `extract_and_register_deps`
  (`calcgraph_session.rs:1009-1014`) collapses to a single
  `!deps.is_empty()`.

M3 (sorted_metadata view)
- New `FunctionRegistry::sorted_metadata()` returning
  `Vec<&FunctionMetadata>` sorted ascending by canonical_name. Mirrors
  the 6.1C H2 deterministic-ordering discipline; the (forthcoming, 6.4)
  `EngineSession::list_functions` mapper reads it at the DTO seam.

M5 (FunctionRegistryError -> EngineError mapper + Appendix A)
- New `map_function_registry_err` in `session.rs` alongside the other
  Appendix-A mappers. Translates `Conflict { name }` -> Conflict /
  `function_exists` and `NotFound { name }` -> NotFound /
  `function_not_found` per contract §10.3. Closed-enum exhaustive
  match (no `_ => unmapped_*` arm). Marked `#[allow(dead_code)]`
  until 6.4-2 wires the trait methods.

Tests
- ql-functions: 4 new substrate-completion tests
  (`sorted_metadata_is_deterministic_across_calls`,
  `isref_carries_lazy_shape_others_carry_address_only`,
  `arg_context_overrides_match_pre_6_4_1_whitelists`,
  `fn_gen_ticks_on_successful_register_and_unregister`).
- ql-exec: `dep_suppressed_reference_fns_match_design` extended to also
  pin LazyShape vs AddressOnly + the typo-guard NOT-LazyShape arm.
- The pre-existing `builtin_metadata_pins_prior_address_only_whitelist`
  test updated for the ISREF -> LazyShape move (pre-6.4-1 it asserted
  ISREF in AddressOnly; now asserts LazyShape).
- Walker invariants
  (`dep_suppressed_reference_fns_match_design`,
  `step_2_reference_aware_names_registered_in_reference_tier`,
  `accepts_special_arg_lists_only_registered_reference_aware_matcher_pin`,
  `every_range_aware_fn_is_admitted_to_is_aggregate_function`,
  `is_aggregate_function_lists_only_registered_aggregates`) updated
  to the new `(registry, name)` signatures.

Verification (focused re-verify of affected lanes)
- cargo check --workspace clean.
- cargo test -p ql-exec --lib: 742/0 (default + --features xlsx-write).
- cargo test -p ql-exec --tests: all integration suites green (no
  per-suite counts changed).
- cargo test -p ql-functions --lib: 1819/0 (1815 pre-6.4-1 + 4 new).
- cargo clippy -p ql-functions -p ql-exec -p ql-session --all-targets:
  clean for edits (pre-existing doc_lazy_continuation +
  type_complexity warns in ql-storage/oplog/collab unchanged).
- node crates/ql-bindings-node/tests/smoke_session.mjs: PASS through
  the freshly-built 6.4-1 cdylib.

Cycle-budget hygiene: this is cycle 1 (code). Cycle 2 (audit) lands in
a separate commit; doc-sync (MASTER-PLAN.md, impl-plan §0,
session-api.md §10, .plans/_active.md, function_meta.rs header,
calcgraph_session.rs module doc, current_work.md, MEMORY.md) follows
as a third commit per established 6.1C / 6.4-0 pattern.

Refs: docs/phase6/6-4-entry-plan.md §2 (block-on-entry must-fix),
docs/audits/2026-05-28-6-4-0-substrate-audit/SYNTHESIS.md (H1 / H3 /
M1 / M3 / M5 / I1 / I2 dispositions), docs/api/session-api.md §10
(function-metadata contract).


